  "passages": [
    {
      "id": "b1.health-and-lifestyle.small-changes",
      "level": "B1",
      "topics": ["health-and-lifestyle"],
      "title": "Small changes, big results",
      "text": "Daniel used to eat fast food almost every day, and he didn't use to do any exercise. He also smoked, and he often stayed up until two in the morning. Last year his doctor told him that he should change his habits. At first Daniel didn't want to listen, but after a few weeks he decided to try. He started by giving up smoking. It wasn't easy, and he almost gave up twice. Then he stopped buying fast food and learned to cook simple meals. Now he enjoys cooking for his friends on weekends. To keep fit, he walks to work instead of driving, and he goes swimming twice a week. He has lost twenty pounds, but the biggest change is in his mood. He gets enough sleep, so he feels less stress at work. \"I don't follow a strict diet,\" he says. \"I just try to make one healthy choice at a time.\"",
      "source": {
        "kind": "original"
      }
    }
  ],
